intermux (3.0.0~beta1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 3.0.0 beta 1 (pre-release): background daemon intermuxd, started
    by systemd when needed, that reports interfaces, routed apps and traffic.
  * New tray intermux-tray with speed limits, Restart and Stop, and
    notifications when a route is lost or restored.
  * The window refreshes on daemon events; new command intermux events.
  * Rust daemon and tray are built and installed; user units and the tray
    desktop entry are added.

 -- Rishi-Bhati <bhatirishi5@gmail.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0530

intermux (2.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 2.2.0: opt-in "Don't ask for my password" through the intermux group and
    a polkit rule, for local active sessions only; sudo intermux passwordless
    on|off turns it on or off.
  * The installers ask once whether to turn it on; --passwordless and
    --no-passwordless answer the question in advance.
  * Security hardening of the root helper: released apps return to their own
    cgroup, users cannot change each other's apps, and helper files get safe
    modes.

 -- Rishi-Bhati <bhatirishi5@gmail.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0530

intermux (2.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 2.1.1: resize arrows only over the gaps between sections.
  * WireGuard VPNs connect on NetworkManager older than 1.42.
  * The DNS check runs in new namespaces with the pre-built bundle.

 -- Rishi-Bhati <bhatirishi5@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0530

intermux (2.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 2.1.0: new main window with tables and inline speed graphs.
  * DNS per interface with custom servers; speed limits; VPN connections from
    the app.
  * Shifted apps keep their DNS, reject IPv6 at once and accept replies under
    strict rp_filter; firewalld trusts each namespace link.

 -- Rishi-Bhati <bhatirishi5@gmail.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

intermux (2.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 2.0.1: keep scanning Firefox profile roots past a symlinked one; security reports go to the Reportary portal.
  * 2.0.0: initial packaging (starting point, untested).

 -- Rishi-Bhati <bhatirishi5@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
